  "query_preview": "..\n(Sunday night through Friday)\nIssued at 215 AM MDT Sat Aug 8 2026\n\nThere isn't much change Monday with the 595dm H5 high center still \nover northern NM. Storm coverage remains focused over northern and \nwestern NM where PWATs continue to rise slightly. QPF footprints\n>0.50\" are still shown over the northern and western high terrain.\n\nChanges may begin by Tuesday as the H5 high shifts eastward into \neastern NM and west TX. This pattern allows for a moist fetch of \nsouth/southeast flow to develop into northwest MX. The upper high \nmay remain centered to the east of NM Wednesday thru Friday while \nabundant monsoon moisture slides north into AZ and NM. PWATs are \nshown rising to near 1.2\" at KABQ with H5 heights decreasing to near \n590dm by Thursday. Model QPF remains bullish mid to late week but\nconfidence is still low to moderate given the stubborn pattern in\nplace the past couple weeks.",
